Subject: [PATCH] Fix FAQ answers that no longer match the live product
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Checked every answer on the live /faq page against actual current
behavior (schema, routes, and UI) and fixed the ones that were wrong:

- "Getting started" claimed email signup exists; only Google/Facebook
  OAuth does (email auth is disabled server-side).
- "Trip editing" and "Trip cancellation" both claimed interested users
  get notified when a trip changes or is cancelled — neither the
  PATCH nor DELETE /api/trips/:id handler notifies anyone.
- "Marking trips complete" described a "Mark Complete" button that
  doesn't exist in the UI (the backend /api/trips/:id/complete +
  notification flow exists but nothing calls it) — rewrote it to
  describe the actual hide/show visibility toggle in Profile > Trips.
- Calendar's "green badges" claim is stylistically wrong post-rebrand
  (ceylon-green now maps to coral, not green) — described functionally
  instead of by color, so it won't drift again.
- "Free trips marked with 💚" is stale — that emoji was removed from
  the Free Trip badge earlier in this rebrand pass.
- Removed an unverifiable "10MB per image" limit claim; the actual
  upload component defaults to 5MB and trip photos don't override it.
- Added a "What's a Quick Trip" entry — the feature wasn't mentioned
  anywhere in the FAQ's 27 questions.

Also removed client/src/pages/faq.tsx, a duplicate FAQ page that was
never routed anywhere (help/faq.tsx is the one both /faq and
/help/faq actually render) and had drifted out of sync with it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
